.TH UOO-BOOT-MANAGER 1 "October 2026" "Uoo Boot Manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uoo-boot-manager \- configure supported Ubuntu boot settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uoo-boot-manager
.RB [ --demo " | " --live ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uoo is a GTK4 desktop for GRUB, UEFI entries, backups, diagnostics, and
supported Ubuntu bootloader repairs. It runs as the current user.
Changes require authentication through the installed administrator helper.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --demo
Use sample configuration without changing system boot data.
.TP
.B --live
Read this computer without automatically falling back to demo mode.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show command-line help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/grub.d/zz-uoo.cfg
Managed GRUB settings.
.TP
.I /etc/grub.d/41_uoo
Managed custom entries.
.TP
.I /var/lib/uoo-boot-manager/backups
Private recovery backups.
.SH AUTHOR
Hayk Jomardyan.
